Message-ID: <Pine.LNX.3.91.960628111158.2173A-100000@marco.internetforce.com>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: TEXT/PLAIN; charset=US-ASCII
Status: RO
X-Status: 


Hi Mike,
how you doing?

We have a problem...
From Internet Force is impossible to reach well.com and from there it is 
impossible to reach Internet Force.
We have some customers that need to comunicate with people there and they 
can't. E-mails don't arrive to destination starting from both side.

Since it is possible to comunicate with well from other Italian and 
American provider, I think there is a problem with the comunication 
between IDT and them.

Look how a traceroute produces:

traceroute well.com
traceroute to well.com (206.15.64.10), 30 hops max, 40 byte packets
 1  firewall.internetforce.com (206.20.95.129)  3.461 ms  3.137 ms  3.18 ms
 2  10.0.1.1 (10.0.1.1)  5.313 ms  5.183 ms  5.314 ms
 3  206.20.64.29 (206.20.64.29)  239.114 ms  271.034 ms  245.904 ms
 4  eth-0.gw-2.nyc.idt.net (199.248.149.253)  179.685 ms  272.603 ms  
184.28 ms
 5  eth-0.gw-2.nyc.idt.net (199.248.149.253)  180.249 ms !H *  181.577 ms !H





traceroute www.well.com
traceroute to www.well.com (206.15.64.12), 30 hops max, 40 byte packets
 1  firewall.internetforce.com (206.20.95.129)  3.306 ms  2.965 ms  2.998 ms
 2  10.0.1.1 (10.0.1.1)  5.103 ms  5.174 ms  5.206 ms
 3  206.20.64.29 (206.20.64.29)  181 ms  183.934 ms  179.063 ms
 4  eth-0.gw-2.nyc.idt.net (199.248.149.253)  180.156 ms  213.972 ms  
180.39 ms
 5  eth-0.gw-2.nyc.idt.net (199.248.149.253)  181.354 ms !H *  191.973 ms !H


Can you please solve this?

thanks,

Marco Iannacone
System Administrator
INTERNET FORCE

