Hi Ira,
how you doing?
I'm writing to you 'cause as I told you it is very urgent for us to have 
those CLASS C I asked you...
As I told you there is this italian provider that wants to change it's 
access provider and buy connectivity from us.
Since the old access provider (the italian IBENET - http://www.ibenet.it) 
is going to cut their line soon, we need to provide them these IP address.

I sent you the information you asked me on the 20th June. Do you have any 
news from InterNIC? When do you think we will receive that addresses?

hope to hear from you soon,
regards,

Marco Iannacone



Wed, 19 Jun 1996, ira rosen wrote:

> No Problem,
> Just send us the list of workstations and a statement of purpose/description
> of what you need that many IPs for.  The internic won't directly give you 15
> class Cs as they are experiencing a shortage of them, in turn this affects  
> the number of class Cs that are distributed to IDT.  Documentation is now   
> required to obtain a class C license.  You may want to include the number of
> workstations that each company will be using (plus the network default 
> and  router IP).  As soon as we recieve this information, we will do our 
> best to obtain 15 class C licenses for you.

Ok.
I send you the actual configuration of one of the company that we have to
sell connectivity to.
It is an Internet Provider itself. Actually they have 10 Class C but they
are not the owner of these address and the owner (the Italian IBENET)
asked to have them back. For this reason we are asking new CLASS C for them.
I'm waiting to have the information back from the other company...
but can you please start asking for these IPs?

Thanks,

Marco Iannacone
System Administrator 
